# Templates CI conventions

## Stages (GitLab)

`validate` → `test` → `security` → `build` → `deploy` → `post-deploy`

## Job files

- One control per file: `secret-scan.yml`, `sast.yml`, etc.
- GitLab: `include: local:` paths; document copy to `.gitlab/jobs/`
- GitHub: reusable `workflow_call` in `workflows/jobs/`

## Gates

- Upload SARIF where supported (`upload-sarif@v4`)
- Run `python scripts/gate-check.py --control <name> --report <file> --policy "$POLICY"`
- Read mode from `config/security-gate-policy.yaml` (`mode: warn|block`)
- Do not use blind `continue-on-error: true` — gate script decides

## Variables

- `REGISTRY` / `SECURITY_POLICY` in entrypoint
- `ENABLE_REAL_LINTERS=true` for opt-in real linters (A2)
- Never `${{ env.* }}` in reusable workflow `with:` blocks — use literals or `github.*`

## Docker (docker-expert)

- Scan all `Dockerfile` and `Dockerfile.*` paths in hadolint jobs
- Emit SARIF via `normalize-sarif.py`; see [docker-production-baseline.md](../../docs/runbooks/docker-production-baseline.md)

## Kubernetes (kubernetes-specialist)

- Helm charts: probes, dedicated ServiceAccount, resource limits, no `:latest` default
- See [k8s-workload-baseline.md](../../docs/runbooks/k8s-workload-baseline.md); run `make validate-helm`

## Mirror rule

Every GitLab job change needs matching GitHub workflow job with same severity contract.
